WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.590
<b>The Superhumans of Enies Lobby</b>

3
00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.120
[LUFFY]
Dumb frog!

4
00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.380
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero?

5
00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.560
[LUFFY]
Don't "gero" me, you big slimy jerk!

6
00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.530
You realize that that slap of yours derailed
our train, don't you?

7
00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:10.900
Froggy!

8
00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:11.800
Turn back!

9
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.040
Get out of the way!

10
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.540
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero!

11
00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.210
We were about to
catch up with Sanji, too!

12
00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:20.310
Now, apologize!

13
00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.140
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero!

14
00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.480
[LUFFY]
Dumb frog!

15
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.600
I'm gonna eat you!

16
00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.940
[PAULIE]
I dunno what's going on out there
right now, but it can't be good!

17
00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.570
Hey, are you guys all right?

18
00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.310
[MOZU]
I guess so.

19
00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.210
Help!

20
00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.840
[LULU]
My back!

21
00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.450
[CHOPPER]
Oh no!

22
00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.000
[ZAMBAI]
Our King Bulls are gone!

23
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.420
They disappeared!

24
00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.160
[KIWI & MOZU]
– No way!
– No way!

25
00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.420
But how?!

26
00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.790
[PAULIE]
No, we're the ones who disappeared.

27
00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:03.260
Our train probably got
derailed back there.

28
00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:06.060
[KIWI & MOZU]
– Whoa, that's even worse!
– Whoa, that's even worse!

29
00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:06.750
[CHOPPER]
What now?!

30
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:07.980
[ZAMBAI]
Hey!

31
00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:08.680
[KOKORO]
Yeah?

32
00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.880
Are we gonna be okay, or what?!

33
00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:15.620
If we can't make it to Enies Lobby,
I'm gonna be really pissed off!

34
00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.650
[KOKORO]
Shut yer trap and gimme a sec!

35
00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.780
I'm trying to work!

36
00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.070
Huh, that's weird.

37
00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.110
Think there's somethin' funny
going on with this current.

38
00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:26.100
Seems like we're stuck.

39
00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.640
[NAMI]
Kokoro?

40
00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.510
Do you know which direction to go?

41
00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:30.780
[KOKORO]
Yeah! Of course I do!

42
00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.600
When we built the Sea Trains we
equipped 'em with Eternal Poses

43
00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.000
set to all the islands
with stations on 'em.

44
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.800
[NAMI]
Then we'll be fine.

45
00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.070
I'll watch the sea-you just steer.

46
00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.000
[KOKORO]
Huh? You sure that'll help?

47
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.400
[NAMI]
I'm a navigator. I got this!

48
00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.270
I see! Huh!

49
00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.170
That's good to know!

50
00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.210
Oh, almost forgot.

51
00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.410
Hey Yokozuna, stop wrasslin'

52
00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:59.620
and get your froggy butt over here!

53
00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.390
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero!

54
00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.900
He ran away!

55
00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:13.300
Gero, gero, gero!

56
00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.000
What was that?

57
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.740
You're glad I'm still okay?

58
00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.110
How sweet!

59
00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:20.810
I know you were just trying
to save me, but you jumped the gun.

60
00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:22.810
These folks didn't kidnap me.

61
00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:23.510
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero?

62
00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:27.720
[CHIMNEY]
Does this mean that
Granny can speak frog?

63
00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:34.460
[ZORO]
What're you guys looking at?

64
00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.930
[ZAMBAI]
That ugly old lady is
talking to a giant frog.

65
00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:38.900
[CHOPPER]
Oh! I get it!

66
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.660
Granny was a frog all along!

67
00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:43.500
She never quite passed
as a human, now did she?

68
00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.540
You realize you guys are gonna
get hit for that later, don't you?

69
00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:47.870
[KIWI]
No kidding.

70
00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.810
[FAMILY MAN]
Hello?! Straw Hat?

71
00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.380
Rocketman?

72
00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:52.640
[FAMILY MAN]
Can you see them yet?

73
00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:53.510
[FAMILY MAN]
No.

74
00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:54.690
I got nothing.

75
00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.960
Damn that stupid frog!

76
00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:00.300
That thing musta sent them
flying a million miles away!

77
00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.000
[FAMILY MAN]
Hey!

78
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.500
Don't start losing hope on me!

79
00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.910
[FAMILY MAN]
We set out to save our bro Franky and
we won't stop till we make it happen!

80
00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:08.040
[FAMILY MAN]
That's right!

81
00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.580
All we can do now is keep on heading
to Enies Lobby and have faith that Rocketman

82
00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.710
is gonna meet us whenever we get there!

83
00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:19.950
[FAMILY MAN]
Go! Sodom! Gomorrah!

84
00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:22.810
Hey! Hold on.

85
00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.690
What's that over there?

86
00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:28.000
It looks like there's another train
car floating just ahead of us!

87
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.900
It could be full of enemies!

88
00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:30.870
All right, guys!

89
00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.350
Let's prepare for battle!

90
00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:34.020
[EVERYONE]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

91
00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:36.950
[FAMILY MAN]
Ahoy!

92
00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.920
Is anyone in there?

93
00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:40.890
We're the Franky Family!

94
00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:42.940
Come out and show yourself!

95
00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:45.110
[FAMILY MAN]
Hey, I see someone!

96
00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:51.570
[FRANKY]
What?

97
00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.580
He's really alive?

98
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.130
<b>Car 1
Puffing Tom</b>

99
00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.940
You're not just yankin' my chain?

100
00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.450
[ROBIN]
No.

101
00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.160
I heard that he still survived.

102
00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:01.590
I see.

103
00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.190
That's good.

104
00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:06.000
Stupid Ice-for-brains.

105
00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.330
Really had me worried
for a while there.

106
00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.470
I thought he was dead for sure.

107
00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.710
For the record, CP9 might
think that they killed him.

108
00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.490
I'd keep quiet about it if I were you.

109
00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:23.480
You act tough but you got a
heart in there like anyone else.

110
00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:31.310
[FRANKY]
Anyway, we're in trouble now.

111
00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:33.320
The government's got
exactly what they want.

112
00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:38.720
The only woman with the know-how
to bring back an ancient weapon

113
00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.720
and the man with the only
known blueprints for one.

114
00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:44.960
Don't that beat all.

115
00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.030
If the government
actually gets that power,

116
00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:49.900
everything's gonna
get turned upside down.

117
00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.800
First they'll end the pirate era.

118
00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:56.650
We won't be able to fight back anymore and
after they're done with us just you wait.

119
00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:59.090
They'll turn their guns
on the rest of the world.

120
00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:03.510
I'm telling you, those ancient weapons
are gonna lead all of mankind to ruin.

121
00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:08.040
My master didn't lay down his life
protecting those blueprints for nothing.

122
00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:13.850
Not if I have anything
to say about it at least!

123
00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:17.490
But still, there's no point in
me making it out of here alone.

124
00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:21.920
You gotta find some way to get
back to Straw Hat, all right?

125
00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.960
[ROBIN]
I can't.

126
00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.810
If I'm with them, it will
only bring them suffering.

127
00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:33.010
[FRANKY]
You're not the one that's hurting them.

128
00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:36.580
Those government bastards may tell
you that your existence is a crime,

129
00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:39.250
but no matter how dangerous you may be,

130
00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:44.750
just being alive, just being
who you are is never wrong.

131
00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.190
[TOM]
Remember, when a ship is built,

132
00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:53.590
no matter what type it's
neither good nor evil, Franky.

133
00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:56.300
[FRANKY]
You got that?

134
00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.670
[LUCCI]
Her very existence has
been nothing but a sin.

135
00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:05.610
[FRANKY]
What you do is your choice but there's
no right or wrong in who you are.

136
00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:16.990
[KOKORO]
My goodness, just look at you!

137
00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:19.790
You're covered in scars!

138
00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:23.530
[KOKORO]
Poor kid.

139
00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:25.270
It's been eight years now.

140
00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:29.640
Eight long years since
Tom was taken away from us.

141
00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:33.010
I've watched you challenge the
sea train every day since then.

142
00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:35.170
Again and again.

143
00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:49.400
[KOKORO]
You were trying to get
stronger, weren't you?

144
00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:55.260
So you won't have to lose
the ones you love ever again.

145
00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.930
So you'll have the
power to protect them.

146
00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.830
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero.

147
00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:02.330
Don't cry.

148
00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:07.800
Now's the time for you to put that
training to the test, big boy.

149
00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:09.770
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero?

150
00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:12.750
[KOKORO]
You remember your
old pal Franky, right?

151
00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.820
He got taken away by the bad guys, too.

152
00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.750
Like Tom.

153
00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:21.690
The good news is, we're on our
way to save him as we speak.

154
00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:25.260
So you up for a fight, or what?

155
00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:28.800
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero Gerooo!

156
00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.340
Hey Straw Hat.

157
00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:32.840
I think I found another friend for ya!

158
00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.440
[LUFFY]
Sounds good to me!

159
00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.420
Nice job, Monster Granny!

160
00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:40.740
Wait or is it Frog Granny?

161
00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.520
You gotta tell me these things!

162
00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.520
Oh?

163
00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:47.200
You call me whatever you like.

164
00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:51.730
[NAMI]
Kokoro, I found us a good current
for running to the southwest.

165
00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:53.530
All right then!

166
00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:59.130
Well we wasted a little time back
there but we'll get it back in a flash!

167
00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.700
[LUFFY]
You heard her, Frog!

168
00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:01.870
Let's go!

169
00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.400
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero!

170
00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.340
[MARINE]
CP9 has arrived!

171
00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:11.310
Look sharp!

172
00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:13.590
<b>Judicial Island
Enies Lobby</b>

173
00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.810
[MARINE]
Congratulations on
completing your mission!

174
00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:14.960
[MARINE]
Bring out the criminals!

175
00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.360
They're in car 1!

176
00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:20.840
[FRANKY]
Hey, how 'bout you handle me

177
00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.150
with a little more care, ya lugheads!

178
00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:26.050
Where I come from, I'm a VIP.

179
00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:27.790
[MARINE]
Whoa, everyone stand back!

180
00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:28.460
[MARINE]
Be careful!

181
00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:30.660
That guy bites!

182
00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:32.500
[FRANKY]
You punks want some of this, huh?!

183
00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:33.970
Must he be so noisy?

184
00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.800
[HATTORI]
Coo coo!

185
00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.400
[MARINE]
I've never seen them up close.

186
00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.860
[MARINE]
Pretty intimidating.

187
00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:48.400
[MARINE]
That guy's Cutty Flam, right?

188
00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.470
[MARINE]
No way, then the woman must be.

189
00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:52.900
Nico Robin?!

190
00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.100
[MARINE]
Wow, she's gorgeous!

191
00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:57.430
[MARINE]
Open the main gate!

192
00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:16.720
Huh?

193
00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:17.520
[FAMILY MEN]
Whoa!

194
00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:20.740
What the hell is this crazy place?!

195
00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.220
A waterfall?

196
00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:32.720
What?

197
00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:43.400
I can't see the bottom!

198
00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.340
[KAKU]
You sure are a noisy one.

199
00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:55.080
[SPANDAM]
It looks like Lucci and the
others are headed this way.

200
00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:04.220
And they've brought me the best
souvenir I could ever possibly wish for.

201
00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:07.890
[SPANDAM]
At last.

202
00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:11.390
After five long years,
the time has finally come

203
00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:15.100
for all eight members
of CP9, to be reunited.

204
00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.870
This should be a time of celebration.

205
00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:21.740
[SPANDAM]
But instead I'll ask,
"What's the meaning of this?"

206
00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:25.690
Your orders were to assassinate
the leaders of the revolution!

207
00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:27.880
But according to this article,
not only did you

208
00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.580
kill those three, but
twenty others, as well!

209
00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:31.550
What happened?

210
00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:33.720
If you have an excuse,
I'd like to hear it!

211
00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:35.390
[KUMADORI]
Yoyoi!

212
00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:39.530
My most sincere apologies
and pardons, Chief!

213
00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:46.370
Everything is entirely,
unreservedly, completely, my fault!

214
00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:50.500
<b>Jabra
Six Powers Master, CP9</b>

215
00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:47.800
[JABURA]
Stop that, Kumadori!

216
00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:50.870
A real man doesn't bow
his head to anybody!

217
00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.340
I'll explain everything
that happened to the Chief,

218
00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.960
<b>Fukuro
Six Powers Master, CP9</b>

219
00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:55.370
so shut up and get a hold of yourself!

220
00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.470
[KUMADORI]
Yoyoi!

221
00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:58.410
I can't apologize enough!

222
00:12:56.510 --> 00:13:00.430
<b>Kumadori
Six Powers Master, CP9</b>

223
00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:04.220
And so if need be I'll shoulder
the blame by taking my own life!

224
00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.550
Don't be so melodramatic!

225
00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:06.270
[KUMADORI]
Yoyoi!

226
00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:07.570
It happened like this, Chief.

227
00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:09.190
We followed the plan to the letter.

228
00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:11.950
We infiltrated their forces and were
all ready for the assassination.

229
00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:15.490
But somehow the enemy managed
to find out about our plans!

230
00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:19.820
[FUKURO]
Probably 'cause I was talking
about them all over town, Chapapa!

231
00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:20.820
You again?

232
00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:21.910
What's wrong with you?

233
00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:23.670
And what's the point in
having a zipper on your mouth

234
00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:25.610
if it you don't even
use the damn thing?

235
00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.810
This little blabbermouth problem
of yours has got to stop, understand?

236
00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:29.680
We're secret agents!

237
00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:30.720
We've got secrets to keep!

238
00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:33.220
[FUKURO]
I didn't do it on purpose, Chapapa!

239
00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:34.520
[JABURA]
Don't you "Chapapa" me!

240
00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:36.690
Can't do anything
about it now, Chapapa!

241
00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:40.510
[KUMADORI]
There's no need to blame Fukurou!

242
00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:44.310
I will take full responsibility!

243
00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:48.610
Seppuku! Iron Body!

244
00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:51.350
I can't even die right!

245
00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:53.350
[JABURA]
Oh just get it over with, you bastard!

246
00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.320
You'd be doing everyone a favor!

247
00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:56.450
I accidentally talked
about it, Chapapa!

248
00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:57.720
[SPANDAM]
Shut up!

249
00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:58.420
[SPANDAM]
Enough.

250
00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:00.590
I understand.

251
00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:01.290
Hot, hot, hot!

252
00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:04.070
I spilt my coffee again, dammit!

253
00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:07.040
Oh, by the way, I heard
Nero didn't work out.

254
00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:08.120
Whatever.

255
00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.440
[FAMILY MAN]
We gotta hurry!

256
00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:18.250
[FAMILY MAN]
Can't you bulls go any faster?

257
00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:28.500
[FAMILY MAN]
So big bro Franky sacrificed
himself to save you guys?

258
00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:29.530
And now he's...?

259
00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:30.430
[SANJI]
Yeah.

260
00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:32.400
That's right.

261
00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:36.370
He was trying to rescue Robin
and help us escape with her.

262
00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:44.300
[FAMILY MAN]
Our Big Bro is such a kind-hearted guy!

263
00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:47.850
We need to hurry or
we won't make it in time.

264
00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:50.650
[FAMILY MAN]
Look!

265
00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:52.420
The lights of the "Nightless Island"!

266
00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:54.420
[FAMILY MAN]
It's Enies Lobby!

267
00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:56.220
[FAMILY MAN]
Really?

268
00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:57.420
I can't believe we made it!

269
00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:58.720
All right!

270
00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:01.190
[FAMILY MAN]
Now we can rescue bro!

271
00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.050
"Nightless Island"?

272
00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:03.880
[FAMILY MEN]
Yeah!

273
00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.680
[FAMILY MAN]
The sun never stops shining there.

274
00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:06.950
So it's "nightless".

275
00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:10.460
They sometimes call the Judicial
Island a "Daytime Island", too.

276
00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:14.110
[LUFFY]
We found them!

277
00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:16.210
The giant yagaras!

278
00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:19.310
Ahoy!

279
00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.080
[BOTH]
– Luffy!
– Luffy!

280
00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:26.520
Hey! Sanji!

281
00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:30.220
[LUFFY]
And...Who the heck it that?

282
00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:35.500
[FAMILY MAN]
It's Straw Hat!

283
00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.600
Looks like we caught up with 'em.

284
00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:39.870
No problem.

285
00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:41.730
[NAMI]
Well, now that we've found the others.

286
00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:44.000
It's time for our date
with the World Government!

287
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.800
[KOKORO]
Hell yeah, it is!

288
00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:52.540
[TILESTONE]
Okay! This is it!

289
00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:54.740
[ZAMBAI]
Now approaching Enies Lobby!

290
00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:55.640
All hands!

291
00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:57.720
Get ready for a showdown!

292
00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.790
[LUFFY & CHOPPER]
– Sniper King from Sniper Island?
– Sniper King from Sniper Island?

293
00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:12.060
For real?

294
00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:13.130
[SOGEKING]
That's right!

295
00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:14.930
I'm a close friend of Usopp's.

296
00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:18.640
I'm here because he asked me to aid
you on this perilous journey!

297
00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:20.680
He's a super hero!

298
00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:21.690
I knew it!

299
00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.890
I could totally tell
'cause of the mask and cape!

300
00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:24.560
Amazing!

301
00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:26.300
I've never seen one before!

302
00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:29.410
[CHOPPER]
So wearing a mask and cape
means he has super powers?

303
00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:30.550
'Course!

304
00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.580
Everybody in a mask
and cape is a super hero!

305
00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:33.450
Really?

306
00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:33.950
Well, yeah!

307
00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.190
[ZORO]
Isn't that Usopp?

308
00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:37.690
[NAMI]
I'm glad you're safe, Usopp.

309
00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:41.200
[ZAMBAI]
That's the long-nose guy that
busted into the Franky House.

310
00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:44.200
[KIWI]
That's the guy that got
taken away with bro.

311
00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:45.000
[MOZU]
Totally.

312
00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.040
No question.

313
00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.000
[LUFFY]
It's... It's nice to meet you!

314
00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.100
[SOGEKING]
Likewise.

315
00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:50.970
[CHIMNEY]
That's one of the guys
we met at the Shift Station.

316
00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:51.730
[GONBE]
Meow!

317
00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:52.870
[CHOPPER]
Can I have your autograph?

318
00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:54.470
[SOGEKING]
Sure.

319
00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.790
"To Sir Chopper"

320
00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:59.750
[LUFFY]
But that makes me
wonder...Where did Usopp go?

321
00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:00.680
[SOGEKING]
He's safe.

322
00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:02.850
There's no need to worry about him.

323
00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:07.710
Anyway, he told me the most important thing
right now is saving your friend Robin.

324
00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:08.710
Then he left.

325
00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:09.490
Yep.

326
00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:10.990
He's absolutely right.

327
00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:15.830
[CHOPPER]
So, uh...So where exactly
is this Sniper Island?

328
00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:17.860
[SOGEKING]
I'll tell you.

329
00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:26.090
It's inside of your heart.

330
00:17:26.090 --> 00:17:26.960
[CHOPPER]
Wow!

331
00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:34.860
[NAMI]
Seriously. Where?

332
00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:41.970
Sing it!

333
00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:45.560
[SANJI]
Hey, Nami.

334
00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:46.790
Huh?

335
00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.330
Yeah? What is it?

336
00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:50.330
Just a second.

337
00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:52.760
The rest of you idiots
should hear this, too.

338
00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:54.260
Before we go to rescue Robin...

339
00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:56.660
There's something you

340
00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.030
So there you have it.

341
00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:10.570
Those CP9 guys are controlling Robin by
using her childhood fears against her.

342
00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:13.970
I'm not making excuses for
not being able to save her.

343
00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:16.140
I just wanted to make it clear
that even if we march in

344
00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:18.240
to get her back, it doesn't
necessarily mean

345
00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.520
that she'll be willing
to return with us.

346
00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:23.680
[LUFFY]
None of that matters!

347
00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.950
I won't stand for this!

348
00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:29.390
Damn Robin!

349
00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:31.030
It's not her fault!

350
00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:32.330
Of course it is, Nami!

351
00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.230
Why doesn't she want us to rescue her?

352
00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:35.300
It doesn't make sense!

353
00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.570
Because she doesn't
wanna feel responsible

354
00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:39.740
for all the awful things that'll
happen to our crew once we do!

355
00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:41.190
[LUFFY]
I don't care about all that!

356
00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:44.020
If we don't rescue her, she's
gonna be killed, isn't she?

357
00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:46.750
There's no way she wants to die,
so we're gonna save her!

358
00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:49.060
Well of course she doesn't
want to die, but still!

359
00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:50.000
[ZORO]
Let it go.

360
00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:53.670
This doesn't change what we have to do.

361
00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:55.170
We'll save her either way.

362
00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:58.310
[LUFFY]
I'm gonna beat up
every last one of them!

363
00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:01.850
There's a new move I wanna try!

364
00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.970
[PAULIE]
Hey, guys, take a look at this.

365
00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:12.790
I came to this island once before
to do some maintenance on the railway.

366
00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:14.850
I drew this from what I could remember.

367
00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:19.830
It's a rough sketch of the
overall layout of Enies Lobby.

368
00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:26.810
The Gates of Justice are located
at the back of the island.

369
00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:29.320
The only way to get to them
is through the Tower of Law.

370
00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:31.920
[LUFFY]
What's that big black thing?

371
00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:33.720
It represents the waterfall.

372
00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:34.660
Huh?

373
00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:35.360
Yeah.

374
00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:37.590
Once we're inside, you'll see.

375
00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:41.030
<b>Iron Fence</b>

376
00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:40.990
<b>Main Gate</b>

377
00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:39.690
[PAULIE]
If we don't rescue
Franky and Nico Robin

378
00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:41.160
before they pass through the Main Gate

379
00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:42.110
<b>Island Gate</b>

380
00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:40.570
<b>Iron Fence Main Gate</b>

381
00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:43.780
and into the Gates of
Justice, then that's it.

382
00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:44.660
<b>Courthouse</b>

383
00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:44.660
<b>Tower of Justice</b>

384
00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.660
<b>Gates of Justice</b>

385
00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:42.410
<b>Island Gate</b>

386
00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:44.910
It's over.

387
00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.250
And why's that?

388
00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:47.510
[LUFFY]
It doesn't matter
where they take her to,

389
00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:50.420
we'll just keep on fighting
them until we get Robin back!

390
00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:53.320
[NAMI]
I explained this before
we left Water 7, remember?

391
00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:55.760
Once we pass that gate,
the only two places

392
00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:58.290
we can go are Navy Headquarters
or the deep-sea prison.

393
00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:02.550
No matter what happens, we have to settle
this before they reach those rear gates.

394
00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.450
[PAULIE]
Yep. Pretty much.

395
00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:08.190
On top of that, even if we all
rushed the island at the same time,

396
00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:12.190
the only ones capable of going
up against those CP9 guys...

397
00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:13.960
– are you Straw Hats.

398
00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:16.930
After seeing what you can do,
I know how strong you are.

399
00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:20.530
That's why I think you should
stay behind once we get there.

400
00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:24.410
Give us five minutes, then charge
through to the main island in Rocketman.

401
00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:27.840
[ZAMBAI]
The Franky Family and Galley-La will go
in first and break open the Main Gate

402
00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:31.120
and the Main Island Front Gate
so the train can pass through.

403
00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.950
I'm sure we'll suffer
a lot of casualties,

404
00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:35.450
but remember: Once you're in,
keep going no matter what.

405
00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:37.720
Don't look back.

406
00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.400
We've only got a little over 60 people.

407
00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:44.440
The enemy forces probably have
somewhere between 2 and 3 thousand.

408
00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:46.570
Our best chance for victory
is for you Straw Hats

409
00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:50.910
to concentrate on CP9 and leave
the rest of the marines to us.

410
00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:52.710
Right, I got it.

411
00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:54.150
[KOKORO]
Okay, folks!

412
00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:57.550
We're pulling up to
the front of the island!

413
00:20:57.550 --> 00:21:01.830
[KOKORO]
While we're here, take a look
at the sky behind Enies Lobby.

414
00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:02.730
Behold!

415
00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:04.930
The Gates of Justice.

416
00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.970
[FAMILY MEN]
Whoa!

417
00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:10.300
That's huge!

418
00:21:13.550 --> 00:21:16.710
It's not a good idea
to open them all the way.

419
00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.820
When it comes time to
send a criminal through,

420
00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:22.050
they only unlatch them
just enough to let 'em pass.

421
00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:24.620
Behind that gate are
some big sea kings.

422
00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:27.250
That part of the sea is
a lot like the Calm Belt:

423
00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:30.600
An eerie body of water cutting
right through the Grand Line.

424
00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.830
No normal ship would
dare to sail there.

425
00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:35.000
They'd be lost forever.

426
00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.430
I don't know how they managed to do it,

427
00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:40.650
but somehow the Navy figured out
a way to make it through safely.

428
00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:45.280
In other words, it's like the pirate girl
said: You can't take back a criminal once

429
00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:46.550
they pass through those gates.

430
00:21:46.550 --> 00:21:50.490
Any chance of a rescue is gonna
have to happen before they open.

431
00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:51.420
Go!

432
00:21:51.420 --> 00:21:52.220
Hop to it!

433
00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:54.290
There's no time to lose!

434
00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:58.690
[ZAMBAI]
We'll head in first and clear a path
for you, just like we planned!

435
00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:01.000
Give 'em hell, Straw Hats!

436
00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.260
[ZORO]
Hey!

437
00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:03.210
You two over there!

438
00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:04.970
Aren't you supposed to be with us?

439
00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:09.480
[CHOPPER]
Hm?

440
00:22:10.170 --> 00:22:12.210
[CHOPPER]
Wait, where's Luffy?

441
00:22:12.210 --> 00:22:12.910
Huh?

442
00:22:12.910 --> 00:22:14.940
He was here just a second ago.

443
00:22:20.470 --> 00:22:21.170
[FAMILY MAN]
Look!

444
00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:23.510
Isn't that Straw Hat?

445
00:22:27.010 --> 00:22:29.310
[EVERYONE]
– What?
– What?

446
00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:31.980
[EVERYONE]
Why the hell is he going in on his own?

447
00:22:32.700 --> 00:22:36.700
That crazy Straw Hat didn't
understand the plan at all!

448
00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:39.010
[NAMI]
There goes our strategy.

449
00:22:39.010 --> 00:22:41.140
[SANJI]
He said "Right! I got it", didn't he?

450
00:22:41.140 --> 00:22:44.060
[SOGEKING]
He's really not the
wait-five-minutes type.

451
00:22:44.060 --> 00:22:45.830
Damn. Should have known.

452
00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:49.440
He's an impatient one, isn't he?

453
00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:50.740
Yeah!

454
00:22:50.740 --> 00:22:52.220
[CHIMNEY]
Go, Mister Pirate!

455
00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:53.350
[GONBE]
Meow!

456
00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:55.820
Gero, gero!

457
00:22:55.820 --> 00:22:56.520
Too late now!

458
00:22:56.520 --> 00:22:57.220
[ZAMBAI]
Let's move!

459
00:22:57.220 --> 00:22:59.460
Sodom! Gomorrah!

460
00:22:59.460 --> 00:23:03.040
Jump over that iron fence and
then break open the main gate!

461
00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:13.990
[LUFFY]
Gum Gum...Rocket!

462
00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:18.500
[MARINE]
What the...?

463
00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:20.510
Something just flew over!

464
00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:24.360
[MARINE]
Whoa!

465
00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:25.830
[LUFFY]
What's up with this place?

466
00:23:25.830 --> 00:23:27.400
What a huge hole!

467
00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.300
It looks like the island's
floating or something!

468
00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:32.000
[MARINE]
There's someone up on the flagpole!

469
00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:35.420
[MARINE]
Shoot him down before he gets away!

470
00:23:35.420 --> 00:23:36.120
[LUFFY]
Whoops!

471
00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:38.890
Guess they spotted me!

472
00:23:40.530 --> 00:23:42.760
[MARINE]
He went inside the main gate!

473
00:23:42.760 --> 00:23:44.830
Get back here!

474
00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:49.300
[MARINE (OVER SNAIL)]
This is the Main Gate!
This is the Main Gate!

475
00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:53.280
I have an urgent message for the Chief
Officer at the Main Island Front Gate!

476
00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:54.450
[MARINE (OVER SNAIL)]
This is the Main Gate!

477
00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:56.980
It's an emergency!

478
00:23:56.980 --> 00:23:58.420
[SPANDAM]
This is Spandam.

479
00:23:58.420 --> 00:23:59.650
What's going on?

480
00:23:59.650 --> 00:24:01.840
[MARINE (OVER SNAIL)]
An intruder somehow managed
to pass through the Main Gate

481
00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:04.130
and is heading toward
the Main Island, sir!

482
00:24:04.130 --> 00:24:04.950
[SPANDAM]
One intruder?

483
00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:06.860
That's what all this fuss is about?

484
00:24:06.860 --> 00:24:08.720
Surely you can manage
to take care of him.

485
00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:09.390
[MARINE (OVER SNAIL)]
But, sir!

486
00:24:09.390 --> 00:24:11.990
[GUARD (OVER SNAIL)]
You don't understand, it's... This
is the Main Island Front Gate.

487
00:24:12.470 --> 00:24:13.870
Intruder sighting confirmed.

488
00:24:13.870 --> 00:24:14.770
Don't worry.

489
00:24:14.770 --> 00:24:16.300
We'll take care of things from here.

490
00:24:19.250 --> 00:24:20.280
[GUARD]
Hey there, buddy!

491
00:24:20.280 --> 00:24:21.310
That's far enough!

492
00:24:21.310 --> 00:24:23.960
[GUARD]
Do you have the slightest
idea where you are?

493
00:24:23.960 --> 00:24:25.660
[MARINE (OVER SNAIL)]
Don't take this guy lightly!

494
00:24:25.660 --> 00:24:28.930
Unless my eyes deceive me,
then I'm pretty sure that he's...

495
00:24:29.860 --> 00:24:31.830
The pirate Straw Hat Luffy!

496
00:24:34.010 --> 00:24:34.710
[GUARDS]
What?

497
00:24:38.170 --> 00:24:39.070
[GUARD]
What was that you just said?

498
00:24:39.870 --> 00:24:42.770
[MARINE]
The man with the
100 million berry bounty!

499
00:24:42.770 --> 00:24:44.070
It is him!

500
00:24:44.070 --> 00:24:45.940
Straw Hat Luffy!

501
00:24:50.980 --> 00:24:52.830
Where's Robin?

502
00:25:06.290 --> 00:25:10.930
[LUFFY]
Tell me where Robin is right now!
